# C8 item 1, ANION model: relaxed scan of C128...O133 (ketone C to HOO- oxygen).
#
# Built from the relay TS (ts/optts_bridge/job.xyz) by deleting {130,131,132,136}:
#   O131 with H130/H136 = the water; H132 = the TRANSFERRING proton (1.11 A to
#   O133, 1.34 A to the water O). H135 stays, so the peroxide is HOO- on O133.
# 137 -> 133 atoms; the water and the relay are gone from the SYSTEM, not demoted
# to MM.
#
# Charge convention (this is the test): the QM region is the anion, so
#   * xyzfile -1 1   -> QM region charge -1 (94 electrons, even, singlet OK)
#   Charge_total -1  -> whole system -1; the GFN-FF host is then 0
# (Previously both were 0 on the xyzfile line and ORCA counted 93 electrons,
# odd, against a singlet -- impossible.)
#
# Relaxed scan of the forming bond, 1.40 -> 2.80 A, to locate the barrier
# maximum. Full system, 17-atom QM1, TightOpt.
! QM/XTB B97-3c ddCOSMO(Water) Opt TightOpt TightSCF

%QMMM
QMATOMS
	{55 58 61 64 120 121 122 123 124 125 126 127 128 129 130 131 132}
END
Charge_total -1
Mult_total 1
AutoFF_QM2_Method GFNFF
END

%geom
  Scan
    B 128 130 = 1.40, 2.80, 15
  end
  MaxIter 200
  # NO Calc_Hess: with Calc_Hess true the scan writes step 1's Hessian as
  # job.001.hess but then tries to read job.hess at step 2 (InHessName: job.hess)
  # and dies with "Error (ORCA_GSTEP): could not find the Hessian file!" after
  # step 1 has already converged. A relaxed scan only needs the model Hessian
  # plus the BFGS update.
end

%output jsonpropfile true end

%maxcore 4000

%pal
   nprocs 8
end

* xyzfile -1 1 job.xyz
